  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Saturday)\nIssued at 115 AM CDT Sun May 24 2026\n\nOn Monday, an upper level low will be centered across northeast \nTexas with another upper level low/trough from the Great Basin into \nthe Desert Southwest. Weak upper level ridging is expected in \nbetween these features, across West Central Texas. This will result \nin dry and warm conditions, with highs in the mid 80s to lower 90s. \nOvernight lows will be in the 60s. \n\nOn Tuesday, the aforementioned upper level trough will approach from \nthe west. This will result in large scale ascent with scattered to \nnumerous showers and thunderstorms developing to our west by mid to \nlate afternoon. Showers and thunderstorms will then track east \nacross the area Tuesday evening into the early morning hours \nWednesday. There is medium to high (60-90%) chance of showers and \nthunderstorms Tuesday into Tuesday night. At this point, locally \nheavy rainfall looks to be the main concern as precipitable water \nvalues increase to 1.5 inches or higher across parts of the area. \nLow to medium (20-70%) rain chances will continue on Wednesday, \nmainly across central and eastern portions of the area. A weak upper \nlevel trough will continue across the region, so expect at least \nscattered mainly diurnally driven showers and thunderstorms. Highs \non Tuesday will be in the low to mid 80s, with highs on Wednesday in \nthe upper 70s to lower 80s. \n\nAs the upper level trough tracks east on Thursday and another more \npotent upper level low develops across the western CONUS, weak upper \nlevel ridging will develop across West Central Texas. This will \nresult in mainly dry conditions on Thursday, with highs back in the \nmid to upper 80s. The large upper level low across the western CONUS \nis then forecast to weaken Friday into the weekend, with a weak \nupper level trough approaching the forecast area. This will likely \nbring an return of at least isolated to scattered showers and \nthunderstorms to the forecast Friday into the weekend.",
